course: dictionary
lesson: 10592
title: Underprivileged and fair chances
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how people's lives are. Underprivileged is one of them. It has two parts: under means less, and privileged means having special advantages. So an underprivileged person has fewer advantages than most people.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The charity helps underprivileged children with books and warm coats.» Helps, books and warm coats show that these children are missing things most children have, so they need help.
explain: Notice the feeling of the word. Underprivileged is a softer word than poor. It talks about chances and advantages, not only money, and it is often used in news, charity and school language.
fact: Underprivileged means having less money, fewer chances and fewer good things in life than most people.
fact: The word is built from parts: under means less, and privileged means having special advantages.
fact: «Underprivileged children» means children who have fewer chances and good things than most children.
fact: «Underprivileged areas» means places where many people have fewer chances and good things.
fact: Underprivileged is a softer word than poor, so it is often used in news, charity and school language.
exercise: What does underprivileged mean? | Being very clever at school | *Having fewer chances and good things than most people | Living near the sea | Having more money and more chances than most people
exercise: In underprivileged, which part means less? | *under | privileged | children | under-privileged
exercise: Ellie says underprivileged means the same as rich. What is wrong with her idea? | It is only used for animals | It means happy and healthy | Rich and underprivileged mean exactly the same | *It means the opposite: having less money and fewer advantages
test: Which word sounds softer in news and charity language? | poor | *underprivileged | hungry
test: «The school runs a club for children from underprivileged areas.» What does underprivileged areas mean? | Places that are very old | *Places where many people have fewer chances and good things | Places under the sea | Places with the most parks and gardens
exam: Which sentence uses underprivileged correctly? | Underprivileged is my favourite colour of paint. | He ran underprivileged around the park. | *The charity helps underprivileged children who have fewer chances. | The underprivileged sky was bright blue and sunny.
